      "text": "To find the integer \\( n \\) such that \\( 0 \\le n \\le 7 \\) and \\( n \\equiv -3737 \\pmod{8} \\), we need to determine the remainder when \\(-3737\\) is divided by 8. \n\nFirst, let's find the remainder of \\( 3737 \\) divided by \\( 8 \\). We do this by using the method of repeated division.\n\n\\[\n3737 \\div 8 = 467 \\quad \\text{with a remainder of} \\quad 3737 - 467 \\cdot 8 = 3737 - 3736 = 1\n\\]\n\nThus, \\( 3737 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{8} \\).\n\nGiven \\( -3737 \\pmod{8} \\), we can use the property of congruence:\n\n\\[\n-3737 \\equiv -(3737) \\equiv -1 \\pmod{8}\n\\]\n\nSince \\(-1\\) modulo 8 is equivalent to 7 because:\n\n\\[\n-1 + 8 \\equiv 7 \\pmod{8}\n\\]\n\nSo,\n\n\\[\n-3737 \\equiv 7 \\pmod{8}\n\\]\n\nThus, the integer \\( n \\) that satisfies \\( 0 \\le n \\le 7 \\) and \\( n \\equiv -3737 \\pmod{8} \\) is\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{7}\n\\]",
