      "text": "1. **Starting with 2 more than the largest modulus (8)**\n   - Begin by adding 2 to the modulus, given as 8. This gives us the range [0, 10].\n\n2. **Identify the integer \\( n \\)**\n   - The problem requires finding the integer \\( n \\) such that \\( 0 \\le n \\le 7 \\). As a result, we limit \\( n \\) to the closed interval [0, 6].\n\n3. **Calculate the remainder**\n   - Now, calculate the remainder \\( r \\) when \\( -3737 \\) is divided by [2, 8]. The calculation proceeds as follows:  \n     \\[\n     r = -3737 \\mod 2\n     \\]\n     - We need to find the value of this remainder within the bounds [0, 6].\n\n4. **Adjust the remainder**\n   - If \\( r \\) is greater than 7, adjust it to bring it within the desired interval [0, 7]. The adjustment process can be simplified to:\n     \\[\n     r = r \\mod 8\n     \\]\n     - This ensures that \\( n \\) remains within the initial specified bounds.\n   - Thus, perform:\n     \\[\n     r = (-3737 \\mod 8)\n     \\]\n\n5. **Convert the determination of \\( n \\) back earlier**\n   - Compare \\( r \\) with 6 (since we are constrained within the range [0, 6]).\n   - If \\( r \\geq 6 \\), adjust it by:\n     \\[\n     n = 6\n     \\]\n     - Otherwise, no need for such adjustment; direct \\( n = r \\) meets the condition.\n\nConclusion:\n\\[\n\\boxed{n = r}\n\\]",
