      "text": "We need to find an integer \\( n \\) that satisfies \\( n \\equiv -3737 \\pmod{8} \\).\n\n1. **Simplify the negative numerator modulo 8:**\n   - First, find the remainder when \\( 3737 \\) is divided by 8.\n\n2. **Calculating the remainder:**\n   - \\( 3737 \\div 8 \\) gives \\( 467 \\) with a remainder, \\( r \\):\n     \\[\n     3737 = 8 \\times 467 + r\n     \\]\n   - Iterate to find the remainder \\( r \\):\n     \\[\n     3737 = 8 \\times 467 + r\n     \\]\n   - Since \\( 8 \\times 467 = 3736 \\), the remainder \\( r \\) from \\( 3737 \\div 8 \\) is:\n     \\[\n     r = 3737 \\mod 8\n     \\]\n   - Calculating manually: \n     \\[\n     3737 \\div 8 = 467 \\text{ remainder } 3\n     \\]\n     Thus,\n     \\[\n     3737 \\equiv 3 \\pmod{8}\n     \\]\n\n3. **Set up the congruence:**\n   - Given \\( -3737 \\equiv r \\) mod 8, substituting the result from above:\n     \\[\n     -3737 \\equiv -3 \\pmod{8}\n     \\]\n   - Since we want \\( n \\) in the range [0, 7], we convert \\(-3\\) back to a positive value within the indicated range by:\n     \\[\n     -3 \\equiv 5 \\pmod{8} \\quad \\text{(as} \\ -3 + 8 = 5 \\)\n     \\]\n\n### Conclusion:\nThe resulting integer \\( n \\) that fits within the range is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{5}\n\\]",
